<main class="pc" data-product-depth="twinmind" data-twinmind><p class="pc-kicker">CRANIO SYSTEMS / TwinMind</p><h1>Your story should not start from zero.</h1><p class="pc-lead">TwinMind is the continuity architecture: experience, context, state, observation, history and the next step.</p><p class="pc-note">Local working prototype · no account</p><div class="pc-chain"><span>Experience</span><i aria-hidden="true">→</i><span>Context</span><i aria-hidden="true">→</i><span>State</span><i aria-hidden="true">→</i><span>Observation</span><i aria-hidden="true">→</i><span>History</span><i aria-hidden="true">→</i><span>Pattern</span><i aria-hidden="true">→</i><span>Next step</span></div><section class="pc-section"><h2>Personal observation journal</h2><p class="pc-note">Records remain in this open page's memory. Save a file and reopen it to continue another day. No automatic transfer, cloud storage or synchronization.</p><p class="pc-note">Do not enter names, diagnoses, documents or other people's personal data. Exported files are not encrypted; store them securely.</p><div data-tm-controls hidden><div class="pc-journal"><div class="pc-card"><form data-tm-form><label for="tm-date">Observation date</label><input id="tm-date" type="date" name="date" required><label for="tm-context">Context (for example, workday)</label><input id="tm-context" name="context" maxlength="300"><label for="tm-observation">What did you notice?</label><textarea id="tm-observation" name="observation" maxlength="2000" required></textarea><div class="pc-actions"><button type="submit">Add observation</button></div></form><label for="tm-import">Open local Navigator, Potential or TwinMind files</label><input id="tm-import" type="file" accept=".json,application/json" data-tm-import><div class="pc-actions"><button data-tm-export type="button">Save history</button><button data-tm-clear type="button">Clear journal</button></div><output data-tm-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></output></div><div class="pc-card"><div class="pc-history" data-tm-list></div></div></div></div><noscript><p>JavaScript is required for the local journal.</p></noscript></section><section class="pc-section"><h2>Continue exploring</h2><div class="pc-actions"><a class="pc-button primary" href="../your-cranium/">Personal Navigator</a><a class="pc-button" href="../potential/">Potential</a><a class="pc-button" href="../cases/">Cases</a><a class="pc-button" href="../start/">Discuss TwinMind development</a></div></section><section class="pc-section"><details class="pc-legacy"><summary>Existing materials</summary><div class="wrap"><article class="article"><div class="crumbs">CRANIO / TwinMind</div><h2>TwinMind</h2><p class="lead">TwinMind is designed to connect experience, context, state, observations and history. Its personal account and persistent history are not connected yet. The website currently explains the model and lets you explore the observation framework.</p><section class="section"><h2>Continue exploring</h2><div class="grid"><a class="card" href="../experience/"><h3>For You</h3><p>Your experience</p></a><a class="card" href="../cases/"><h3>Cases</h3><p>What a useful record contains</p></a><a class="card" href="../method/"><h3>Method</h3><p>Observe → Calibrate → Identify → Optimize → Verify</p></a></div></section><div class="actions"><a class="btn dark" href="../start/">Start</a></div></article></div></details></section><script type="application/json" data-tm-strings>{"confirm":"Remove all entries from the current journal?","empty":"No records yet.","invalid":"Could not read file: unsupported format or limit exceeded.","added":"Observation added.","loaded":"File processed.","removed":"Record removed.","delete":"Remove","duplicate":"Duplicate records skipped.","own":"Personal observation","snapshot":"Imported snapshot","unrated":"Not rated"}</script></main>